 "text": "Hey, nice to hear from you. How are you? That's completely normal. The key is to look interested and engaged rather than overwhelmed. Pick one dish you really like, and ask the waiter about it. That gives them chance to tell a story and it' less intimidating. Dress smart casual, not too smart, and don't worry about shoes. People usually wear jeans and sneakers. Ask the waiter to explain, or look it up first. Most places have pictures and short descriptions so you' not alone. If you' nervous, that's fine. Most of the time, the chef will give you something amazing anyway. If you do order, start with one or two things, and ask about each as you go.",
